.TH MU2EDAQ-RUNLOG-DB.YAML 5 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-runlog-db t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq-runlog-db.yaml \- run-log viewer configuration files and variables
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I config/default.yaml
.br
.I config/development.yaml
.br
.I config/production.yaml
.br
.I .env
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I runlogdb/settings.py
builds the Django settings in this order, later sources winning:
.IP 1. 4
.I .env
in the checkout, loaded with python-dotenv
.BR "override=False" :
a variable already present in the process environment is
.B not
replaced.
.IP 2. 4
.IR config/default.yaml .
.IP 3. 4
.IR config/ "<DJANGO_ENV>" .yaml ,
deep-merged over the default.
.B DJANGO_ENV
defaults to
.BR development .
.IP 4. 4
.B RUNLOGDB_*
environment variables for the keys listed below.
.PP
.BR start\-mu2e\-rundb\-viewer (1)
exports
.B DJANGO_ENV=development
before Django starts when the variable is unset, so a
.B DJANGO_ENV
line in
.I .env
never takes effect through the start scripts.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B database.backend
.B sqlite
or
.BR postgres .
Default
.BR sqlite ;
.B postgres
in
.IR production.yaml .
Env
.BR RUNLOGDB_DB_BACKEND .
.TP
.B database.sqlite.path
Relative to the checkout.
Default
.IR db.sqlite3 .
No env override.
.TP
.BR database.postgres.host ", " .port ", " .name ", " .user ", " .password
Defaults
.BR localhost ,
.BR 5432 ,
.BR runlogdb ,
.BR runlog ,
empty.
Env
.BR RUNLOGDB_DB_HOST ,
.BR RUNLOGDB_DB_PORT ,
.BR RUNLOGDB_DB_NAME ,
.BR RUNLOGDB_DB_USER ,
.BR RUNLOGDB_DB_PASSWORD .
No schema or
.B search_path
setting exists; table names are unqualified.
.TP
.B auth.enabled
Default
.BR true ;
.B false
in
.IR development.yaml .
Env
.BR RUNLOGDB_AUTH_ENABLED .
When false,
.I runlogdb/middleware.py
logs every request in as a superuser named
.BR dev .
When true, django-allauth is active and its local
.I /accounts/signup/
endpoint is open to anyone (see
.BR mu2edaq\-runlog\-db (7)).
.TP
.BR auth.providers.fermilab_cilogon. { client_id , client_secret , oidc_endpoint }
OIDC provider labelled "Fermilab CILogon".
.B oidc_endpoint
defaults to
.BR https://kc.apps.okddev.fnal.gov/realms/myrealm ,
a development Keycloak realm.
Env
.BR RUNLOGDB_FERMILAB_CLIENT_ID ,
.BR RUNLOGDB_FERMILAB_CLIENT_SECRET ;
no env override for the endpoint.
.TP
.BR auth.providers.google. { client_id , client_secret }
Env
.BR RUNLOGDB_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID ,
.BR RUNLOGDB_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET .
Any Google account is accepted.
.TP
.B github.token
Personal access token used by the bug-report page to create issues.
Env
.BR RUNLOGDB_GITHUB_TOKEN .
.TP
.B github.repo
Default
.BR Mu2e/mu2edaq\-runlog\-db .
Env
.BR RUNLOGDB_GITHUB_REPO .
.TP
.B app.debug
Default
.BR false ;
.B true
in
.IR development.yaml .
Env
.BR RUNLOGDB_DEBUG ;
any value other than
.BR 0 ,
.BR false ,
.B no
or
.B off
is true.
.TP
.B app.secret_key
Default
.BR change\-me\-before\-deploying ,
also used in production unless
.B RUNLOGDB_SECRET_KEY
is set.
Nothing checks that it was changed.
.TP
.B app.allowed_hosts
Default
.BR "[localhost, 127.0.0.1]" ,
inherited by production;
.B ["*"]
in
.IR development.yaml .
No env override.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Besides the
.B RUNLOGDB_*
variables above:
.TP
.B DJANGO_ENV
Overlay name.
.TP
.BR RUNLOGDB_HOST ", " RUNLOGDB_PORT
Bind address and port, read by the start script, not by
.IR settings.py .
.B RUNLOGDB_PORT
is also the port announced by the discovery responder.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .env.example
Template for
.IR .env ;
.I .env
is git-ignored.
.SH EXAMPLES
A production environment, exported before starting:
.PP
.RS
.nf
export DJANGO_ENV=production
export RUNLOGDB_SECRET_KEY="$(python3 \-c 'import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(50))')"
export RUNLOGDB_DB_HOST=db.example RUNLOGDB_DB_NAME=runlogdb
export RUNLOGDB_DB_USER=runlog RUNLOGDB_DB_PASSWORD=...
\&./start\-mu2e\-rundb\-viewer
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start\-mu2e\-rundb\-viewer (1),
.BR manage.py (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-runlog\-db (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ group, Fermilab.
